var $author$project$Route$Guide$CompositionTextField$native = 'Two things make this safe. First, **native HTML is first-class and typed.** `TypedHtml.input` is a real `<input>`, but its attributes are closed to the ones an input actually permits — `type_`, `placeholder`, `name`, `value`, `checked`… An input has no `href`, so `TypedHtml.input [ TypedHtml.Attributes.href "/x" ]` is a **compile error**, not a raw-HTML escape hatch. You get the exact tag you asked for, with the exact attributes it\'s allowed.\n\nSecond, **the library never injects.** It assembles the pieces you wrote — it doesn\'t secretly wrap, reorder, or add structure around your content. What you write is what renders. A search field is the same move with a different input `type_`; once you can compose one field, you can compose any of them.';
var $author$project$Route$Guide$CompositionTextField$recap = '- There\'s no `M3e.TextField` — a field is **composed**: form field + typed native `<input>` + a label wired by one shared id.\n- **Native HTML is typed**: an `<input>` with an `href` doesn\'t compile.\n- The library **assembles, never injects** — what you write is what renders.\n- **Next: [Generated & inspectable](/guide/generated-and-inspectable) →** you\'ve built real things on this API; now see why you can trust it — it\'s generated, and inspectable data underneath.';
