var $author$project$Route$Guide$Seams$intro = 'Everything you write on top of the library is **userland** — your own code. Most of it needs no escape at all: standard HTML is already typed (`TypedHtml.div`, `TypedHtml.label`, …), and "custom" content usually just fills a component\'s *typed slot*. A **seam** isn\'t something you build — it\'s the *practice* of reaching for the library\'s own fenced escapes, `M3e.Unsafe` and `M3e.Unsafe.Attributes`, instead of improvising a way around the type system. They ship in one lint-guarded place so every real crossing is loud, named, and greppable — no userland adapter module required. This page shows the two things worth telling apart: a genuine escape (`modelViewer`, below) and typed code that only looks like one (`twoColumn`, `linkNav`).';
